{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120200-new-horror-little-morpheus","id":1120200,"title":"[New Horror] Little Morpheus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-24T20:15:24-07:00","id":1120200,"title":"[New Horror] Little Morpheus","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sometimes, when people find themselves wishing for a friend or someone to give them advice, they experience strange and vivid dreams of a tree house among the stars. Inside this place a boy lives among his books and toys. He welcomes visitors with great enthusiasm and politeness, and uses his immense power over the dreamscape to accommodate and entertain them as best as he can. Soon enough, he asks to become friends with the visitors and embark on a dream quest with him. When they ask for his name, he introduces himself as \u201cLittle Morpheus\u201d and lists a bunch of both mighty and whimsical titles such as \u201cGuardian Of All Dreams\u201d and \u201cMayor Of Sleepytown\u201d. He does not elaborate on his exact nature or origins, but tries to make such quests into profound learning experiences for his friends. However, while he is not foolish or forceful by any means, his understanding of the world is childlike in most regards. He is very glad to help, but can only guide them so far. What the dreamers make of the journey is entirely up to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Little Morpheus is of a vague age, but no more than late teens. He is short but athletic, with tanned skin from playing beneath the sun so much. His hair is curly and dirty blond, often with a twig or a leaf in it. His ears and nose are big and goofy, but not as much as his smile, which is charming enough to win the hearts of even the grumpiest adults. He wears simple hiking clothes, but around his neck is a scarf that is like a piece of the midnight sky. In dreams, he favors outfits with celestial motifs and displays a crown like the rising sun. When flying, he stands on a fluffy white cloud.<br /> <br /> <b>Little Morpheus, Royal Avatar Of The Stargazer</b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5 (Goetia)<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 13, Finesse 15, Resistance 15<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 50<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 15<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 13<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 33<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>24<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 5/0<br /> <b>Melee Damage Bonus:</b> +5L<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Dreams 5, Friendship 3, Hope 3<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Discorporate, Dreamwalker, Image, Materialize<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Adventure's Elixir, Countermagic, Dreamshaping, Gift Of Flight, Hallucination, Know Soul, Mortal Mask, Occult Sight, Omen Trance, Sign, Strings Of Fate<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171004-ten-spirits-binded?p=1172094#post1172094\"><b>Noble Numina:</b></a> Dream Invasion, Dream Throne, Investiture Of Power, Mass Influence x 1 (Dreams), Panoply x 2 (+Rank To Corpus And Armor, +Rank To Melee Damage Bonus), Web Of Power<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only use Influences or Numina to help someone who is suffering from a Condition that represents severe psychological or spiritual damage, such as Broken, Fugue or Madness.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> An object covered in the blood of someone who willingly ruined their greatest friendship while pursuing their dreams<br /> <br /> <b>Adventure's Elixir:</b> As per the Miracle Dread Power. However, it can only be used to remove and apply Conditions and Tilts that are mental or spiritual. Furthermore, instead of destroying one of the target's Aspirations, this Numen changes the target's Long Term Aspiration to reflect their engagement with and interpretation of a dream quest given by Little Morpheus. The resulting Long Term Aspiration is not selected by Little Morpheus, but shaped by the target's own thoughts and emotions regarding the dream quest. The character does not have conscious control over this, but the player and ST should work together to decide a meaningful goal to reflect the character development. Any given character can only benefit from this Numen once per Story.<br /> <br /> <b>Countermagic:</b> The entity is more resilient against Supernal and Abyssal magic. By spending 1 Essence, it may use Resistance instead of Rank to Withstand such magic during this turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamshaping:</b> Requires Dreamwalker Manifestation. This Numen gives Influence 5 (Dreams). Look to Changeling: The Lost and its supplements for possible inspirational material regarding this Influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamwalker:</b> (Requires Open Condition) By spending 2 Essence, the entity shifts from Twilight into the Dream Space of an individual or location with the Open condition, or vice versa. Once there, it can interact with the Dream Space in the same way it interacts with the real world (including other entities also active in the Dream Space), and may use Influences and Numina.<br /> <br /> <b>Gift Of Flight:</b> Little Morpheus may fly at 5 times his ground Speed at will, and applies his Defense against ranged attacks when doing so. He may extend this Numen to living or inanimate targets for the scene through touch and by spending 1 Essence. He can choose to let living targets control their flight with Dexterity + Athletics + his Rank rolls, or control it himself with Finesse + Rank rolls. Doing the latter to living targets requires winning a Power + Finesse vs Stamina + Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance roll. The maximum Size of any target is equal to his Resistance.<br /> <br /> <b>Know Soul:</b> As per the Dread Power.<br /> <br /> <b>Occult Sight:</b> Little Morpheus is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. He notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of his senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Essence, he can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using his Finesse + Rank as his dice pool. Lastly, he always knows when he is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>Strings Of Fate:</b> As per the Fate 4 spell. Spend 3 Essence and roll Power + Finesse vs Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance as an Instant Action. This Numen is considered to include the Reach options for line of sight and for presenting opportunities each day instead of each week. The effect lasts for one day per Success. Supernatural attempts to undo this Numen trigger a Clash Of Wills against Finesse + Rank.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-26-2019, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T10:42:38-07:00","id":1120404,"title":"","content":"Awesome Horror; I quoted it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1120403#post1120403\">here</a> to consolidate it in a thread where other horrors can be found. Like the Geotia summoning ability, that's incredibly potent as a tool for pulling people into an adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-25-2017, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T10:47:09-07:00","id":1120407,"title":"","content":"I have my suspicions but what was the inspiration for this &quot;Horror&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T10:57:49-07:00","id":1120410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120200-new-horror-little-morpheus?p=1120404#post1120404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome Horror; I quoted it <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1120403#post1120403&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> to consolidate it in a thread where other horrors can be found. Like the Geotia summoning ability, that's incredibly potent as a tool for pulling people into an adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks a lot! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:05:21-07:00","id":1120417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120200-new-horror-little-morpheus?p=1120407#post1120407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my suspicions but what was the inspiration for this &amp;quot;Horror&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> The inspirations were Little Nemo In Slumberland, the Little Prince, Nanny McPhee, the Greek God Morpheus and a not sociopathic Peter Pan.<br /> <br /> This is not really a Horror. It's actually an Enigma, which is a term that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> coined to described creatures which have the Horror template but are not actively malevolent or scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T12:43:40-07:00","id":1120447,"title":"","content":"I can imagine a Cabal of Mages coming together after being guided through an Astral journey that was their Awakening by this Enigma, and them coming to believe the enigma is capable of Awakening Sleepers when in actuality it was the mage's own predisposition to not accept the Lie that made them such vivid dreamers and promising adventure partners and ultimately why they were chosen for the journey.<br /> <br /> Being a Mystery that Mage's want to solve can be an aggravating situation even if you're an immortal untrappable demigod, being one that Mage's believe can reliably Awaken people is likely going to require just enough unpleasantness to deter people from being overly proud concerning Little Morpheus.<br /> <br /> I can see this being becoming very angry with unethical Mages attempting to control or study him via dissection/vivisection/confinement/compulsion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T14:23:50-07:00","id":1120484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120200-new-horror-little-morpheus?p=1120417#post1120417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The inspirations were Little Nemo In Slumberland, the Little Prince, Nanny McPhee, the Greek God Morpheus and a not sociopathic Peter Pan.<br /> <br /> This is not really a Horror. It's actually an Enigma, which is a term that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> coined to described creatures which have the Horror template but are not actively malevolent or scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nailed it. Glad to know I used the quotations right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T18:08:13-07:00","id":1120566,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Little Morpheus</b><br /> <br /> I like this write up - it present a character that is good and innocent, but powerful enough that any creature of darkness would need to think twice before tangling with him!<br /> <br /> Excellent write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T18:35:26-07:00","id":1122160,"title":"","content":"I love it-lovely little excursion into some of the high weirdness that shows that not everything supernatural is out to get you. Some of it even friendly!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T19:57:28-07:00","id":1195089,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Little Morpheus is now an Ephemeral Being instead of a Horror, check the first post again for details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-28-2018, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}